{"kind":"stack","id":"s-conductors","title":"Conductors and insulators","theme":{"background":"#f4f9ff","foreground":"#1b2a41","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Conductor"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-d","content":"A material that lets electricity or heat travel through it easily."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Insulator"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-d","content":"A material that does not let electricity or heat travel through it easily."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which material is a good conductor of electricity?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Copper","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Rubber","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Plastic","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which material is an insulator?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Glass","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Iron","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Aluminium","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Most metals are good conductors of electricity. Which metal is this?"},{"type":"image","picto":"bulb"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Gold","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Wood","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Cotton","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"You are fixing a lamp. Which tool do you pick to hold the wire?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Metal pliers","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Plastic-handled pliers","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The metal pliers carry the electricity and give you a small shock. Good to know: metal conducts!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"The plastic handles are insulators, so the electricity stays in the wire and you stay safe."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Why are electrical wires covered in plastic?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Plastic is an insulator, so it keeps the electricity inside the wire","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Plastic is a conductor, so it carries the electricity further","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Plastic makes the wire heavier so it stays on the ground","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which of these is a good conductor of heat?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"A metal spoon","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"A wooden spoon","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"A plastic spoon","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished conductors and insulators."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Metals are good conductors and many other materials are insulators. Keep looking for them around you."}],"actions":[]}}
